  "rationale": "Focused knockout library (178 colon-cancer MPRA putative target genes plus common-essential controls, 6 guides each, 100 safe-targeting guides) screened in DLD1, HCT116 and SW948. The three deposited per-line count files (guide IDs sgNNN-<gene>, columns sample_N) are merged by guide ID in prepare.R, which adds the Gene column; sample_N maps to GSMs through the GSM titles ('DLD1 tumor rep 1 (sample_1)', 'DLD1 Day 0 (sample_11)', ...). The paper's Supplementary Table 6 gives MAGeCK results per line for subcutaneous tumours (DLD1, HCT116, SW948) and 2D culture (DLD1, HCT116); the comparison reference is not stated in the accessible text, and day 0 is assumed (10 tumours vs 2 day-0 libraries; 2 2D vs 2 day-0). Tumours are independent xenografts, not paired with day-0 replicates, so no replicate term. SW948 2D is analysed for completeness (no published table). Controls: 100 safe-targeting guides (cutting controls). SW948 tumour rep 2 (sample_42) is left out: 27% of its guides have zero reads (a bottlenecked tumour; Spearman 0.26 with day 0 versus 0.38-0.55 for the other tumours), and the published SW948 log fold changes match a median-normalized tumour-vs-day-0 LFC without it (r = 0.96) but not with it (r = 0.74), so the paper evidently excluded it too. For DLD1 and HCT116 the published MAGeCK LFCs correlate 0.98 with tumour-vs-day-0 LFCs and ~0 with tumour-vs-2D, confirming day 0 as the reference.",
  "counts_md5": "761c4c1398aec5fb208bde0ec66c237a"
